※ pl4g-test: module
※※ A type with code of its own, for a program beside this one.

※※ What a bag holds.
@[export]
type Bag = held: u8

※※ Twice what it holds, reached as `m.Bag.doubled`.
※
※ The only three-part path the language has: a module, a type it exports, and a
※ name belonging to that type.  There is never a fourth -- a type's own file is
※ where what belongs to it is written.
@[export]
fn Bag.doubled(b: &Bag) → u8:
    b⌖.held + b⌖.held

※※ And one that is not exported, which a file importing this cannot write at all.
fn Bag.hidden(b: &Bag) → u8:
    b⌖.held
